---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href, lessonPath, playgroundPath, PLAYGROUNDS } from '../../site';

const pg = PLAYGROUNDS.find((p) => p.slug === 'explorer')!;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title={pg.title} description={pg.summary} current={playgroundPath(pg.slug)} wide>
  <p class="eyebrow">Playground</p>
  <h1>{pg.title}</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Singer's construction needs no search, so it scales. Pick any prime power q up to 1024 and a background thread
    writes down a (q² + q + 1, q + 1, 1) difference set: for q = 1024 that is 1,025 numbers out of 1,049,601. The
    picture draws a chord between every two members; the tally checks every one of the differences, and each nonzero
    residue turns up exactly once.
  </p>
  <div data-widget="large-q-explorer" data-q="101" data-url-state></div>
  <p>
    The set is the list of i for which the trace of α<sup>i</sup> is zero, where α generates the field with q³
    elements, exactly as in <a href={href(base, lessonPath('14-writing-down-a-difference-set'))}>Lesson 14</a>. The
    link in your address bar keeps q, so you can share a view. For why the search in the <a
      href={href(base, playgroundPath('search-vs-construction'))}>search versus construction</a> playground can't
    reach these sizes, see <a href={href(base, lessonPath('17-every-planar-set-singer'))}>Lesson 17</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
